# T-001: Initialize Project Knowledge

## Goal

Replace template placeholders with the first concrete project brief, scope,
non-goals, success criteria, and next ready task.

## Context

The generated project starts in definition. The owner must replace placeholders
with concrete project knowledge before product implementation starts.

## Scope

- Update project brief, requirements, roadmap, and generated status dashboards.
- Keep the first task small and focused on project knowledge.

## Out of Scope

- Product implementation.
- Production runtime.
- External services or infrastructure.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `project/brief.md` names the problem, target user, desired outcome, scope, non-goals, assumptions, risks, and success criteria.
- [ ] `project/roadmap.md` has at least the active milestone updated for this project.
- [ ] `project/requirements.md` contains only concrete and verifiable requirements for the current scope.
- [ ] `make sync-project-docs` and `make validate-project` pass.

## Verification

Run:

```bash
make sync-project-docs
make validate-project
```

## Documentation Impact

Project knowledge documents and generated dashboards will be updated.

## Completion Notes

Pending.

## Notes

Do not implement product code before the ready-for-development gate passes.
